          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef ridge_svd_df_and_rmse(X_train, y_train, X_test, y_test, lam: float) -> tuple[float, float]:\n    X_tr = np.asarray(X_train, dtype=float)\n    X_te = np.asarray(X_test, dtype=float)\n    y_tr = np.asarray(y_train, dtype=float)\n    y_te = np.asarray(y_test, dtype=float)\n    mu, sd = X_tr.mean(axis=0), X_tr.std(axis=0)\n    X_tr_s, X_te_s = (X_tr - mu) / sd, (X_te - mu) / sd\n    y_bar = float(y_tr.mean())\n    U, s, Vt = np.linalg.svd(X_tr_s, full_matrices=False)\n    df_eff = float(np.sum((s ** 2) / (s ** 2 + lam)))\n    beta = Vt.T @ ((s / (s ** 2 + lam)) * (U.T @ (y_tr - y_bar)))\n    rmse = float(np.sqrt(np.mean((y_te - (y_bar + X_te_s @ beta)) ** 2)))\n    return (round(df_eff, 4), round(rmse, 4))\n```"
